A||||4||88formula||Some pictures of my car under construction||||2||
Z||000000||88formula||05-12-2001||11:15 PM||||Here is a picture of Rodney Dickmans Clutch shaft bushing tool. I could have made my own but for $15 it was worth it because I didn't have to waste my time finding the right sized pipe to make one. Every time I buy something from this guy I am impressed with the quality and service I get. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rodneys_tool_resized.JPG"> <BR>Here is a picture of the engine bay. A high performance 210 horsepower 3.4-liter engine is going back in place of the old 2.8. Dynos will be coming in the future along with track results.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine_bay_resized.JPG"> <BR>Man I miss my fiero! It's been almost a year now and I can't remember how it drove anymore. All I do remember is that it was a blast to drive. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Back_of_car_no_eng_resized.JPG"> <BR>This thing just looks awesome even though there is something missing here.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_of_car_no_eng_resized.JPG"> <BR>Here is a picture of the engine cradle with the transmission and suspension. It has KYB struts, all new polyurethane bushings, new brakes and reconditioned calipers, and new wheel bearings. The exhaust you see is a Borla exhaust system. The piece in the back in my own fabricated cat eliminator pipe and the bends are mandrel bends. The springs are stock because I like the nice ride it has and don't want to ruin that. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine_cradle_&_exhaust_resized.JPG"> <BR>   <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||2
Z||000001||Fformula88||05-13-2001||11:43 AM||||Everything is looking great so far!  I bet you miss it, but it won't be long and you'll be cruising around again!  In fact, with those 210 ponies, you may never stop driving it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||05-13-2001||03:29 PM||||I remember when my car was powered by "Fred's feet"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> couldn't wait until I got it on the road  so I know how you're feeling.  Looks great, keep us informed of progress and track times!!!<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||05-13-2001||03:35 PM||||Good luck, I wish I had the time and $ to take everything out and clean/repaint. It looks verry nice.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000004||88formula||05-13-2001||08:34 PM||||Here is a picture of the reconditioned calipers. Was going to purchase reconditioned calipers until I saw the $140 price tag each and decided to get the old manual out and do them myself. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Rear_Brake_calipers_resized_1.JPG"> <BR>The previous owner drove the car with the emergency brakes on and cooked the rear brakes. They were so bad that when I removed the pads they just fell apart. I can't believe they were in this condition because they still stopped the car a lot better than the new brakes in my old 87 coupe.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Rusted_brake_pad_resized.JPG"> <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
